multichoice[40]{tags,text,exhibit,correct,w1,w2,w3,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.1|objective:cisco:300-435:1.1|topic:yang","Which YANG statement makes a node hold a value that must exist elsewhere in the data tree?",,"leafref","typedef","grouping","augment","A leafref points to another node, and its value must match an existing value there. typedef defines a type, grouping defines reusable nodes, and augment extends another module.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.2|topic:aci","Which contract scope lets EPGs in different VRFs of the same tenant use the contract?",,"Tenant","VRF","Application profile","Global","The scope of a contract decides where it applies: within a VRF, an application profile, a tenant, or globally. Tenant scope covers several VRFs of one tenant, VRF scope stays within one VRF, and global scope reaches beyond the tenant.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.3|topic:dpu","Why can a DPU enforce east-west security policy without using the host's CPU?",,"Traffic passes through the DPU's own processors, which run the policy","The host CPU is replaced by the DPU entirely","The policy is stored in the host's BIOS","The DPU copies traffic to the cloud for inspection","A DPU sits in the data path and has its own processing, so filtering and encryption run there. It does not replace the host CPU, and policy is not stored in the BIOS or sent to the cloud.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|objective:cisco:300-435:1.2|topic:netconf","What is the difference between close-session and kill-session in NETCONF?",,"close-session ends the client's own session, while kill-session ends another session","close-session ends all sessions, while kill-session ends one","kill-session ends the own session, while close-session ends another","They are the same operation under two names","A client uses close-session to end its own session gracefully and kill-session to force another session to end, for example to release a lock. They are different operations.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|topic:gnmi","Which gNMI Set operation removes a node from the configuration?",,"delete","update","replace","subscribe","A Set request can carry delete, replace and update lists. Delete removes the node, replace overwrites a subtree, update merges values, and subscribe is a different RPC.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|objective:cisco:300-435:1.5|topic:pyang","Which pyang option limits how many levels of the module tree are printed?",,"--tree-depth","--tree-path","--tree-print-groupings","--tree-line-length","--tree-depth limits the number of levels. --tree-path shows one subtree, --tree-print-groupings includes groupings, and --tree-line-length sets the output width.",1,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.1|topic:gitops|topic:git","Which repository setting prevents engineers from pushing directly to the main branch?",,"Branch protection that requires merge requests","A larger repository quota","A shorter commit message limit","A read-only runner","A protected branch can require review and passing checks before changes are merged. Quotas, message limits and runner settings do not control who can push.",2,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.1|topic:gitops","Why is rolling back a change simple in a GitOps workflow?",,"A revert commit restores the previous declared state, and the pipeline deploys it","The devices keep a copy of the previous configuration in Git","The reconciler deletes the repository","Rollback needs a manual login on every switch","The repository holds every declared state, so a revert commit returns to an earlier one and the same pipeline applies it. Devices do not keep Git copies, and no manual work is needed.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Which Jinja2 filter converts a Python dictionary into JSON text?",,"tojson","json","dump","stringify","The tojson filter serializes a value as JSON, which suits payloads rendered from data. The other names are not Jinja2 filters.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Which Jinja2 environment option removes the first newline after a block tag?",,"trim_blocks","lstrip_blocks","keep_trailing_newline","autoescape","trim_blocks removes the newline after a block tag, which keeps rendered configuration free of blank lines. lstrip_blocks removes leading spaces, and the others have other effects.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible|topic:ndfc","Which module of the cisco.dcnm collection sends an arbitrary API request to the controller when no dedicated module exists?",,"dcnm_rest","dcnm_raw","dcnm_http","dcnm_call","The dcnm_rest module sends a request to a path of the controller's API. The other names are not modules of the collection.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible|topic:aci","Which state of a cisco.aci module returns existing objects without changing anything?",,"query","present","absent","merged","The query state reads objects, present creates or updates them, and absent deletes them. merged is the state of resource modules on other platforms.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|topic:terraform","Which command shows the attributes that Terraform stores for one resource?",,"terraform state show ADDRESS","terraform output","terraform graph","terraform fmt","state show prints the stored attributes of the resource at the address. output shows output values, graph draws dependencies, and fmt formats files.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|topic:terraform","What does a Terraform workspace provide?",,"A separate state for the same configuration","A separate set of providers","A copy of the repository","A faster plan","Workspaces keep several states for one configuration, for example for different fabrics. They do not change providers or copy the repository.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|topic:ansible|topic:troubleshooting","A task over ansible.netcommon.httpapi cannot connect to the controller on the expected port. Which variables should be checked?",,"ansible_httpapi_port and ansible_httpapi_use_ssl","ansible_become and ansible_user only","ansible_python_interpreter","ansible_ssh_pipelining","The httpapi connection uses its own variables for the port and for TLS, so a wrong value there prevents the connection. The other variables concern SSH and privilege.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|topic:terraform|topic:troubleshooting","Terraform plans to create a VRF that someone deleted on the controller by hand. Why does it do that?",,"The refresh finds that the object no longer exists, so it differs from the declared configuration","Terraform stores a backup of every object","The provider has restored the object already","The state file was encrypted","During a plan Terraform compares the configuration with what the provider reads. A missing object is a difference, so it plans to create it again. The other explanations do not apply.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|topic:ncclient","What does device_params={'name': 'nexus'} do in an ncclient connection?",,"It selects the device handler for NX-OS","It sets the hostname of the switch","It chooses the NETCONF port","It enables the candidate datastore","The device handler adapts ncclient to platform specifics, and nexus is the one for NX-OS. It does not set names, ports or datastores.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|topic:ncclient|topic:netconf","Which filter type selects nodes with an XPath expression, provided that the server supports it?",,"xpath","subtree","regex","glob","NETCONF has subtree filters and, with the xpath capability, XPath filters. Regular expressions and glob patterns are not NETCONF filters.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap","A POAP script finds that the checksum of the downloaded image does not match its .md5 file. What should it do?",,"Discard the image and try the download again or abort the process","Install the image anyway","Delete the .md5 file and continue","Change the checksum to match","A mismatch means that the file may be damaged or changed, so it must not be installed. The script retries or aborts, and it never edits the checksum.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap","Which DHCP client information lets the server recognize a POAP switch by its serial number?",,"The client identifier","The vendor class only","The hostname option","The domain name option","The POAP DHCP client puts the switch's serial number in the client identifier, which the server can use to select options per device. The other fields do not carry the serial number.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|topic:guest-shell","Which NX-OS command shows the state of the Guest Shell?",,"show guestshell","show bash-shell","show python","show virtual-service list only","show guestshell reports whether the container is activated and its resources. The other commands do not exist for this purpose.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|objective:cisco:300-435:2.7|topic:python|topic:on-box","Where must an on-box Python script be stored so that the python command can run it?",,"In bootflash or volatile","In the running configuration","In the NVRAM only","On the DHCP server","Scripts run from the switch's file systems, such as bootflash or volatile. The configuration and the DHCP server do not hold files for the interpreter.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.4|topic:ndfc|topic:templates","Which feature lets one Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller template be reused with different values for different switches?",,"Template variables","Backup files","VRF lites","Fabric groups","Variables are the placeholders that a policy fills with values, so a single template serves many switches. Backups, VRF lites and fabric groups are different features.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.5|topic:ndfc|topic:templates","Which contentType does a template of Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller use when its content is CLI?",,"TEMPLATE_CLI","TEMPLATE_JSON","TEMPLATE_PYTHON","TEMPLATE_XML","The template properties name the content type, and TEMPLATE_CLI is used for CLI content. The other values are not content types for CLI templates.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Which field of an NX-API CLI reply contains the result code of a command?",,"code","status","rc","result","In an NX-API CLI reply each output holds code, msg and body, and the code is 200 on success. The other names are not fields of the output.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","How can an engineer try NX-API requests in a browser before writing a script?",,"With the NX-API sandbox that the switch serves over HTTP or HTTPS","With the Guest Shell only","By editing the startup configuration","By opening a console session","The switch offers a sandbox web page to build requests and see their replies. The Guest Shell, the startup configuration and the console are not used for that.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:2.4|topic:cml|topic:simulation","Which element of a CML lab connects it to a physical network?",,"An external connector","An unmanaged switch only","A node definition","A topology file","An external connector bridges the lab to a real network or provides NAT access. An unmanaged switch connects nodes inside the lab, and node definitions and topology files describe the lab.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:3.4|objective:cisco:300-435:4.1|topic:pyats","How can a pyATS command be limited to one device of the testbed?",,"With the --devices option","By deleting the testbed file","By editing the switch's configuration","By using a different Python version","The --devices option selects which testbed devices a command uses. The other options do not select devices.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.3|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|topic:telemetry|topic:mdt","Which telemetry model suits a receiver behind a firewall that allows only outbound connections from the switches?",,"Dial-out, where the switch opens the connection to the receiver","Dial-in, where the collector opens the connection to the switch","SNMP polling from the collector","A syslog server on the switch","In a dial-out model the switch initiates the connection, which passes a firewall that blocks inbound connections. Dial-in and polling need inbound access.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.3|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|topic:telemetry|topic:mdt","What is a sensor path in model-driven telemetry?",,"The path of the data to stream, in the data model of the device","The network path from the switch to the collector","The cable between two switches","The route to the NTP server","A sensor path names the data that is streamed, for example a YANG or DME path. It is not a network route or a cable.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:gnmi","Which TCP port does the gNMI service of NX-OS use unless another port is configured?",,"50051","830","443","57000","The gRPC agent of NX-OS listens on port 50051 by default. 830 is NETCONF, 443 is HTTPS, and 57000 is a common collector port.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:gnmi|topic:tls","A gnmic client gets a TLS verification error against a switch that uses its default gRPC certificate. What are two valid ways to proceed?",,"Install a trusted certificate with grpc certificate, or use --skip-verify in a lab","Switch to port 830","Disable feature grpc","Use plaintext with --insecure on the same port","The default certificate is self-signed, so the client must trust a proper certificate, or skip verification in a test. Port 830 is NETCONF, and the gRPC service of NX-OS uses TLS, so a plaintext connection does not work.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.5|topic:source-of-truth|topic:netbox","What prevents a NetBox record and the configuration of a Nexus fabric from drifting apart?",,"Making changes in NetBox, deploying from it, and running a regular comparison","Editing the switches by hand","Copying the switch configuration into NetBox every week","Disabling the NetBox API","Intent lives in the source of truth, deployments follow it, and a comparison finds drift. Manual edits and copies make the record follow the devices.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nxapi","Which NX-OS command does a script send through NX-API CLI to read interface error counters?",,"show interface counters errors","show running-config","show ip route","show clock","This command reports error counters for interfaces. The others show configuration, routes and time.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nexus-dashboard","How can a long-running script keep working after its Nexus Dashboard token expires?",,"Refresh the token before it expires or log in again, or use an API key","Increase the number of requests per second","Disable TLS verification","Send the password with every request in the URL","Tokens have a limited lifetime, so the script renews it or logs in again, and an API key is an alternative for scripts. The other options do not solve expiry.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","Which command lists the VLAN IDs that are configured on the ports of a Linux bridge?",,"bridge vlan show","ip route show","ip neigh show","ethtool -k","bridge vlan show prints the VLAN configuration of bridge ports. Routes, neighbors and offload settings are different.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|topic:ai","Which task is a good fit for an AI assistant when automating NX-OS?",,"Drafting a first version of a Jinja2 template that is then reviewed and tested","Deploying changes to production without review","Storing the switch passwords","Replacing the source of truth","An assistant is useful for drafts that a human reviews and tests. Unreviewed deployments, secret storage and replacing records are poor uses.",2,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.2|topic:ai|topic:ai-security","Which control best limits the commands that an AI agent can send to a Nexus switch?",,"An allow list of read-only show commands","A longer system prompt","A larger context window","A higher temperature","An allow list is enforced by code, so the agent cannot send other commands. A longer prompt, a larger window or randomness do not restrict anything.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|topic:mcp","Which transport suits an MCP server that several remote clients must reach over the network?",,"HTTP","stdio","A named pipe on the switch","SMTP","An HTTP transport serves remote clients, while stdio is for a local subprocess. A pipe on the switch and SMTP are not MCP transports.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|topic:ai|topic:validation","Why should AI-generated NX-OS configuration be tested on virtual Nexus nodes before it is used?",,"The nodes show how the configuration behaves, which review alone cannot prove","The nodes make the configuration shorter","The nodes translate it to another platform","The nodes remove the need for peer review","Running the configuration shows its real effect and reveals errors, while review checks intent. The nodes do not shorten, translate or replace review.",3,2

multiselect[40]{tags,text,exhibit,c1,c2,c3,w1,w2,w3,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.1|objective:cisco:300-435:1.1|topic:yang","Which two benefits do YANG models bring to network automation? (Choose two.)",,"The structure and types of the data are machine-readable","Payloads can be validated against the model before they are sent",,"Every device returns the same CLI text","No authentication is needed","Configuration is applied without any transport","A model describes data precisely, so tools can generate and validate payloads. It does not standardize CLI text, authentication or the transport.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.2|topic:aci","Which two statements about ACI VRF enforcement are correct? (Choose two.)",,"In an unenforced VRF, EPGs can communicate without contracts","vzAny represents all EPGs of a VRF so that one contract can apply to all of them",,"In an enforced VRF, all EPGs communicate without contracts","vzAny represents a single endpoint","Unenforced mode deletes the contracts","Unenforced mode switches off contract enforcement for the VRF, and vzAny groups all EPGs of a VRF for contract purposes. Enforced mode needs contracts, and nothing is deleted.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.3|topic:dpu","Which two characteristics distinguish a DPU from a basic network interface card? (Choose two.)",,"It has its own programmable processor cores","It can run services such as stateful filtering and encryption",,"It has no memory","It can only forward frames without inspection","It replaces the server's power supply","A DPU combines network interfaces with processing cores that run infrastructure services. A basic card only moves frames.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|topic:grpc","Which two features of gRPC do gNMI and gNOI use? (Choose two.)",,"Multiplexed streams over HTTP/2","Bidirectional streaming between client and server",,"XML-encoded messages over SSH","One new TCP connection for every message","Messages that carry SNMP traps","gRPC runs over HTTP/2, which multiplexes streams and allows streaming in both directions. XML over SSH describes NETCONF, and SNMP traps are a different mechanism.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|objective:cisco:300-435:1.2|topic:netconf","Which two are base operations of NETCONF? (Choose two.)",,"get-config","edit-config",,"Subscribe","Capabilities","Set","NETCONF defines operations such as get-config and edit-config. Subscribe, Capabilities and Set are RPCs of gNMI.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:gnmi|topic:yang","Which two items does a gNMI Set update need? (Choose two.)",,"The path of the node","The value to write, in an encoding that the device supports",,"The IP address of the collector","A sample interval","A subscription ID","An update names the node and the value, and the value must use a supported encoding. Collectors, intervals and subscription IDs belong to streaming.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.1|topic:gitops","Which two items belong in a GitOps repository for a data center fabric? (Choose two.)",,"The data files that describe the intended configuration","The templates and playbooks that turn the data into configuration",,"The passwords of the switches in clear text","The running configuration of every switch as the only source","The log files of past runs","The repository holds intent as data and the code that applies it. Secrets belong in a vault, running configurations are state, and logs are outputs.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.3|topic:gitops|topic:gitlab-ci","Which two checks belong in a merge request pipeline of a network repository? (Choose two.)",,"Linting of the YAML and template syntax","A render test that compares the output with an expected configuration",,"Deployment to production","Deleting the previous branch","Restarting every switch","The merge request pipeline validates the change before review, with syntax and render tests. Deployment comes after the merge.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Which two techniques avoid a trailing comma after the last item in a rendered list? (Choose two.)",,"The loop.last test inside the loop","The join filter on the list",,"The upper filter","The default filter","The length filter","loop.last identifies the final item, and join puts separators only between items. upper, default and length do not control separators.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Which two statements about Jinja2 macros are correct? (Choose two.)",,"A macro takes arguments and can have default values","A macro can be imported from another template",,"A macro runs on the switch","A macro cannot return text","A macro replaces the need for variables","Macros are reusable template functions that can be imported. They render text on the control node and still use variables.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible|topic:aci","Which two ways can the cisco.aci modules authenticate to the APIC? (Choose two.)",,"With a username and password","With a signature made from a private key",,"With an SSH key to each leaf","With a DHCP lease","With an SNMP community","The modules talk to the APIC's API, which accepts passwords and signature-based authentication. SSH keys to leaf switches, DHCP and SNMP are not used.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible|topic:nexus-dashboard","Which two Ansible collections can manage Nexus Dashboard and its fabric controller service? (Choose two.)",,"cisco.nd","cisco.dcnm",,"cisco.ios","cisco.meraki","cisco.dnac","cisco.nd covers Nexus Dashboard, and cisco.dcnm covers NDFC, formerly DCNM. The others target IOS, Meraki and Catalyst Center.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|topic:terraform","Which two commands change the state without changing real objects? (Choose two.)",,"terraform state mv","terraform state rm",,"terraform destroy","terraform apply","terraform import","state mv renames an address in the state, and state rm makes Terraform forget an object. destroy and apply change objects, and import adds an object to the state from the real world.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|topic:terraform","Which two ways pass a value to a Terraform variable? (Choose two.)",,"The -var option on the command line","A terraform.tfvars file",,"A comment in the configuration file","The name of the workspace","The size of the state file","Variables get values from the command line, variable files and environment variables. Comments, workspace names and state sizes do not carry values.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|topic:ansible|topic:troubleshooting","Which two actions help to see what an Ansible module sent to a controller? (Choose two.)",,"Run with -vvv","Register the result and print it with the debug module",,"Increase the number of forks","Disable fact gathering","Run the playbook twice","Verbose output shows the connection and the request, and a registered result shows what the module returned. Forks, facts and repeated runs do not.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|topic:terraform|topic:troubleshooting","Which two causes make a Terraform apply to a controller fail with an authorization error? (Choose two.)",,"The account's role does not allow the operation","The credentials in the provider block are wrong",,"The configuration file uses tabs","The state file is too small","The resource names contain letters","An authorization error comes from the controller and relates to the account or its role. File format, state size and names do not cause it.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|topic:ncclient","Which two ncclient attributes or calls help to find out what a NETCONF server supports? (Choose two.)",,"The server_capabilities of the manager","A get_schema request, when the server supports it",,"The edit_config call","The close_session call","The lock call","The capabilities that the server sent in its hello are in server_capabilities, and get_schema retrieves YANG modules. The other calls change or end sessions.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|topic:ncclient|topic:netconf","Which two statements about an ncclient manager used in a with block are correct? (Choose two.)",,"The session is closed when the block ends","Exceptions of the server can be caught around the calls inside the block",,"The session stays open until the script is restarted","Errors of the server are never raised","The block prevents any configuration change","The context manager closes the session on exit, and server errors raise exceptions that the script can catch. It does not keep sessions open or stop changes.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap","Which two DHCP options does POAP use to learn where the script is? (Choose two.)",,"Option 66 or 150 for the server","Option 67 for the file name",,"Option 6 for DNS","Option 43 for a controller","Option 121 for routes","POAP learns the server from option 66 or 150 and the script name from option 67. DNS, controller strings and routes are not used for that.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap","Which two tasks can a POAP script do? (Choose two.)",,"Download and install a software image","Download a configuration file chosen by the serial number",,"Reconfigure the DHCP server","Change the firewall of the controller","Order new hardware","The script runs on the switch and provisions it with an image and a configuration. It does not manage the server or the controller.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|topic:guest-shell","Which two statements about the Guest Shell of NX-OS are correct? (Choose two.)",,"It is a Linux container that runs beside NX-OS","It can be used to install and run Python packages",,"It replaces NX-OS","It runs only when the switch is powered off","It has no network access at all","The Guest Shell is a separate container with its own Linux environment, which allows more tools. It runs alongside NX-OS and can use the network.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|topic:bash","Which two actions are possible from the Bash shell of NX-OS? (Choose two.)",,"Run Linux commands such as ls on the bootflash","Run a shell script from the bootflash",,"Change the VLANs of other switches","Edit the DHCP server","Reboot the fabric controller","Bash gives access to the Linux environment of the switch and to files in bootflash. Other devices and servers are out of reach.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.4|topic:ndfc|topic:templates","Which two statements about policies in Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller are correct? (Choose two.)",,"A policy is created from a template","A policy can be attached to one or more switches",,"A policy is a Python script that runs on the controller only","A policy can have no template","A policy is stored on the switch only","Policies instantiate templates with values and are applied to switches. They are not scripts or switch-only objects.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.5|topic:ndfc|topic:templates","Which two kinds of variables can a template of Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller declare? (Choose two.)",,"A string","An integer",,"A CLI prompt","A switch serial number only","A VLAN of the data plane","Template variables have types such as string and integer, which the user fills in. The other options are not variable types.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Which two statements about NX-API REST are correct? (Choose two.)",,"It uses a login call to obtain a session cookie","It addresses objects of the switch's object model by their DN",,"It sends CLI text in the body","It is served by the Guest Shell","It uses NETCONF over port 830","NX-API REST authenticates with aaaLogin and addresses managed objects. CLI text belongs to NX-API CLI, and it is served by the switch itself.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Which two benefits does NX-API give over screen scraping a CLI session? (Choose two.)",,"Structured data in JSON or XML","Requests over HTTP that are easy to send from any language",,"No authentication","Faster hardware","No need to enable the feature","NX-API returns structured data and works with ordinary HTTP clients. It still needs authentication and the feature.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.1|topic:cml|topic:simulation","Which two checks fit a simulated Nexus fabric? (Choose two.)",,"Whether the configuration is accepted and the neighbors come up","Whether a routing or VXLAN control-plane change behaves as expected",,"The maximum forwarding rate of the hardware","The power usage of the line cards","The temperature of the data center","A simulation shows configuration and protocol behavior. Hardware rates, power and temperature need real equipment.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:3.4|objective:cisco:300-435:4.1|topic:pyats","Which two outputs can pyATS learn and parse return? (Choose two.)",,"Structured data that scripts can compare","Output that can be saved to a file",,"A changed device configuration","A new device image","A DHCP lease","Parsing and learning produce structured data that can be stored and compared. They do not change the device.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.3|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|topic:telemetry|topic:mdt","Which two properties describe model-driven telemetry data? (Choose two.)",,"It is structured according to a data model","It can be delivered periodically or on change",,"It is plain unstructured text","It can only be polled once an hour","It cannot include counters","Telemetry follows a model and can be streamed on a schedule or when values change. It is not free text and not limited to polling.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:gnmi|topic:grpc","Which two commands help to verify the gNMI setup on a Nexus switch? (Choose two.)",,"show run grpc","show grpc gnmi service statistics",,"show vlan","show cdp neighbors","show clock","The gRPC configuration and the statistics of the gNMI service confirm that the service runs and is used. The other commands show unrelated information.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:telemetry|topic:grpc","Which two values must a destination group of a dial-out subscription contain? (Choose two.)",,"The address and port of the receiver","The protocol and the encoding",,"The VLAN of the receiver","The serial number of the switch","The MAC address of the gateway","A destination names where to send and how: address, port, protocol and encoding. VLANs, serial numbers and gateway MACs are not part of it.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.5|objective:cisco:350-901:2.6|topic:source-of-truth|topic:netbox","Which two data items are best held in a source of truth for a data center fabric? (Choose two.)",,"The intended VLANs and VRFs per tenant","The planned IP prefixes and device roles",,"Interface counters of the last minute","The current CPU load","Live BGP session states","Intended design data is authored and drives configuration. Counters, load and sessions are operational data.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nxapi","Which two commands give a script information about hardware health of a Nexus switch? (Choose two.)",,"show environment","show module",,"show vlan brief","show ip arp","show banner","The environment and module commands report power, fans, temperature and line cards. The other commands report VLANs, ARP entries and a banner.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nexus-dashboard","Which two practices make a Python script that polls Nexus Dashboard well behaved? (Choose two.)",,"Reuse the session and the token between calls","Handle errors and retry with a pause",,"Log in again for every request","Ignore every error","Poll as fast as possible","Reusing the token avoids unnecessary logins, and error handling with a pause keeps load low. The other practices waste resources or hide problems.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","Which two commands help to find out in which VLAN a container's traffic leaves a host? (Choose two.)",,"ip -d link show, to see VLAN subinterfaces and their IDs","tcpdump -e -nn, to see the tags on the wire",,"ip route show only","arp -a only","uname -r","The detailed link output shows VLAN IDs of subinterfaces, and a capture with link-layer headers shows the tag of the frames. Routes and ARP entries do not show tagging.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","Which two statements about veth pairs are correct? (Choose two.)",,"The two ends can be placed in different network namespaces","Traffic that enters one end leaves the other end",,"A veth pair has only one end","A veth pair connects two physical switches","Both ends must be in the same bridge","A veth pair is a virtual cable with two ends, often one in a container and one on the host. It does not need to be in one bridge.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.1|topic:ai","Which two practices make AI-generated templates safer to use? (Choose two.)",,"Render them with sample data and compare the output","Review them like code written by a colleague",,"Deploy them directly","Remove the tests","Hide them from version control","Generated templates still need rendering tests and review. Skipping tests, deploying directly and hiding the code remove safeguards.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.2|objective:cisco:300-435:5.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.2|topic:ai|topic:ai-security","Which two items should not be placed in a prompt that goes to an external model? (Choose two.)",,"Passwords and API keys","Complete running configurations that contain secrets",,"A generic question about a YANG model","The documented syntax of a public command","A made-up example topology","Secrets and configurations with secrets must stay inside. General questions, public documentation and invented examples are safe.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|topic:mcp","Which two things does an MCP client learn from a server when it lists the tools? (Choose two.)",,"The name and the description of each tool","The input schema of each tool",,"The server's password","The source code of the tool","The route table of the switch","A tool listing contains the information that the model needs to call it: name, description and schema.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|topic:mcp|topic:ai-security","Which two measures protect an MCP server that reads data from a fabric controller? (Choose two.)",,"Use a read-only account for the connection","Return only the fields that the task needs",,"Use the controller's administrator account","Return the full database","Disable authentication on the server","Least privilege and data minimization limit the harm of a misled agent. Administrator rights, full data and no authentication increase it.",3,2

match[40]{tags,text,exhibit,p1,r1,p2,r2,p3,r3,p4,r4,p5,r5,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.1|objective:cisco:300-435:1.1|topic:openconfig|topic:yang","Match each part of an OpenConfig interface model to its meaning.",,"config","Writable intended values","state","Read-only operational values","interface","List entry that is identified by its name","counters","Statistics below the state container","description","A leaf with free text","OpenConfig separates intended and operational data into config and state containers, and a list entry is addressed by its key.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.2|topic:aci","Match each ACI bridge domain setting to its effect.",,"L2 unknown unicast: flood","Unknown destinations are flooded in the domain","ARP flooding","ARP requests are flooded instead of being forwarded as unicast","Hardware proxy","Unknown unicast goes to the spine proxy","Unicast routing","The bridge domain routes between its subnets and other networks","Subnet","A gateway address that the fabric provides","The settings decide how the bridge domain forwards unknown traffic and whether the fabric acts as the gateway.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.3|topic:dpu","Match each term used with DPUs to its meaning.",,"Offload","Moving work from the CPU to dedicated hardware","Line rate","Processing at the full speed of the port","East-west traffic","Traffic between servers inside the data center","Stateful firewall","A filter that tracks connections","Encryption offload","Doing cryptography in the DPU","The terms describe what a DPU takes over and the kind of traffic that it handles.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|topic:grpc","Match each gRPC term to its meaning.",,"Channel","The connection to a server","RPC","A call to a remote method","Metadata","Key-value headers, such as credentials","Deadline","The time limit of a call","Stream","A sequence of messages in one call","These terms describe how gNMI and gNOI clients talk to a switch over gRPC.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|topic:gnoi","Match each gNOI service to its purpose.",,"System","Reboot, ping, traceroute and time","File","Get, put and remove files","OS","Install and activate an operating system","Cert","Manage certificates","Factory reset","Return the device to its default state","gNOI groups operational tasks into services that clients call over gRPC.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:gnmi|topic:yang","Match each gnmic subcommand to its purpose.",,"capabilities","Shows the models and encodings of the target","get","Reads values","set","Writes values","subscribe","Streams updates","generate","Creates paths or configuration from YANG models","gnmic offers a subcommand for each gNMI RPC and a helper that works from YANG models.",1,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.1|topic:git|topic:gitops","Match each branching approach to its description.",,"Trunk-based","Short-lived branches that merge into main often","Feature branch","One branch for each change, merged after review","Release branch","A branch that stabilizes a version for release","Hotfix branch","A branch for an urgent fix of a released version","Long-lived branch","A branch that lives for a long time next to main","The approaches differ in how long branches live and what they are for.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.3|topic:gitops|topic:gitlab-ci","Match each pipeline stage of a network repository to its purpose.",,"lint","Checks syntax and style","test","Renders templates and compares the output","plan","Shows what would change","apply","Deploys the change","verify","Checks the result after the deployment","The stages move from checks through a preview to the deployment and its verification.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Match each Jinja2 test to what it checks.",,"is defined","The variable exists","is none","The value is None","is string","The value is text","is number","The value is a number","is iterable","The value can be looped over","Tests check a property of a value, which guards templates against missing or wrong data.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Match each Jinja2 statement to its use.",,"extends","Builds a template on a base template","block","Marks a part that child templates can replace","include","Inserts another template at this place","import","Loads macros from another template","set","Assigns a value to a variable","The statements support inheritance, reuse and variables in larger template sets.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible","Match each Ansible collection to the platform it manages.",,"cisco.nxos","NX-OS switches","cisco.aci","The APIC of an ACI fabric","cisco.dcnm","Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller","cisco.nd","Nexus Dashboard","cisco.mso","Nexus Dashboard Orchestrator","Each collection is aimed at one platform, from single switches to controllers and the orchestrator.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible","Match each Ansible command to its use.",,"ansible-doc -l","Lists the available modules","ansible-doc cisco.nxos.nxos_vlans","Shows the documentation of one module","ansible-inventory --graph","Shows the inventory as a tree","ansible-config dump","Shows the active configuration settings","ansible-lint","Checks playbooks against best practices","These commands help to find modules, read their options, inspect the inventory and settings, and check playbooks.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|topic:terraform","Match each Terraform state command to its effect.",,"terraform state list","Lists the resources in the state","terraform state show","Shows the attributes of one resource","terraform state mv","Renames or moves a resource address","terraform state rm","Removes an object from the state without destroying it","terraform state pull","Prints the current state as JSON","The state subcommands inspect and change the state without touching the real objects.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|topic:terraform","Match each Terraform file to its usual content.",,"main.tf","Resources and providers","variables.tf","Declarations of input variables","outputs.tf","Declarations of output values","terraform.tfvars","Values for the variables",".terraform.lock.hcl","Locked versions of the providers","The usual layout separates resources, inputs, outputs, values and provider locks.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|topic:ansible|topic:troubleshooting","Match each Ansible error message to its likely cause.",,"HTTP Error 401","The credentials are not accepted","SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED","The certificate of the controller is not trusted","Connection timed out","The controller cannot be reached","No module named 'requests'","A Python dependency is missing on the control node","Template syntax error","A Jinja2 expression is not valid","Each message points to credentials, trust, reachability, dependencies or template syntax.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|topic:terraform|topic:troubleshooting","Match each Terraform error to its likely cause.",,"Invalid index","An element that does not exist is addressed in a list or map","Provider configuration not present","A provider was removed while resources of it remain in the state","Missing required argument","A mandatory attribute was left out","Inconsistent dependency lock file","The provider versions changed and init must run again","Invalid for_each argument","The value is not known until the apply","The messages point to a wrong reference, a removed provider, a missing attribute, version changes and values that are not known in advance.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|topic:ncclient","Match each ncclient exception to its cause.",,"AuthenticationError","The login was refused","SSHError","The SSH connection could not be set up","RPCError","The server returned an error for a request","TimeoutExpiredError","The server did not answer in time","OperationError","An operation could not be carried out","The exceptions separate login problems, transport problems, server errors and timeouts.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|topic:ncclient|topic:netconf","Match each ncclient manager call to its NETCONF operation.",,"lock","Locks a datastore","unlock","Releases the lock","commit","Commits the candidate configuration","discard_changes","Throws away uncommitted edits","validate","Checks a configuration without applying it","These calls manage datastore locks and the candidate workflow of a NETCONF server that supports it.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap","Match each POAP component to its role.",,"DHCP server","Gives the address, the server and the script name","TFTP or HTTP server","Serves the script, the image and the configuration","POAP script","Python code that the switch runs to provision itself","Image .md5 file","Lets the script verify the image","conf.<serial>","A device-specific configuration file","POAP needs a DHCP server and a file server, and the script uses checksums and serial-based file names to provision the right software and configuration.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|topic:python|topic:on-box","Match each exception of the NX-OS cli module to its meaning.",,"cli_syntax_error","The command is not valid NX-OS syntax","cmd_exec_error","The command ran but did not succeed","structured_output_not_supported_error","clid cannot give JSON for this command","data_type_error","A value has a type that the function does not accept","getenv","A function that reads an environment value","The module raises specific errors for bad syntax, failed commands, missing JSON support and wrong types.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|topic:guest-shell","Match each Guest Shell command of NX-OS to its effect.",,"guestshell enable","Installs and activates the Guest Shell","guestshell run bash","Starts a Bash session in the container","guestshell disable","Stops the Guest Shell","guestshell destroy","Removes the Guest Shell and its data","show guestshell","Shows the state of the Guest Shell","The commands manage the life of the container and give access to it.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.4|topic:nexus-dashboard","Match each Nexus Dashboard component to its role.",,"Nexus Dashboard","The platform that hosts the services","NDFC","Fabric controller service for NX-OS fabrics","NDI","Insights service for analytics and assurance","NDO","Orchestrator for several fabrics and sites","API gateway","The single entry point for the APIs of the services","Nexus Dashboard is the platform, and the services run on it and are reached through its gateway.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.5|topic:ndfc|topic:templates","Match each property of an NDFC template to its meaning.",,"name","The name of the template","supportedPlatforms","The platforms that can use it","templateType","Whether it is a policy or a profile","contentType","The kind of content, such as CLI","description","A free text","The properties describe what the template is, where it applies and what its content is.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Match each NX-API REST element to its meaning.",,"/api/aaaLogin.json","Logs in and returns a session cookie","/api/mo/sys.json","A managed object, here the system","/api/class/l1PhysIf.json","All objects of the class of physical interfaces","imdata","The list of objects in the reply","query-target=children","Returns the children of an object","NX-API REST addresses objects by DN or by class and returns them in imdata.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Match each field of an NX-API CLI request to its meaning.",,"version","The NX-API version","type","The kind of command, such as cli_show","chunk","Whether the output is chunked","sid","The session ID for chunked replies","input","The command text","The fields select the kind of command, the command itself, and how long output is delivered.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.2|topic:cml","Match each CML node state to its meaning.",,"DEFINED_ON_CORE","The node is defined but not started","STARTED","The node has been started and is booting","BOOTED","The node has finished booting","STOPPED","The node is stopped and keeps its disk","QUEUED","The node waits for resources to start","The states follow a node from definition to a booted system, and stopping keeps its disk.",1,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:3.4|objective:cisco:300-435:4.1|topic:pyats","Match each pyATS command to its purpose.",,"pyats run job","Runs a job file","pyats parse","Parses the output of one command","pyats learn","Learns a feature from several commands","pyats diff","Compares two snapshots","pyats validate","Checks a testbed or other files for errors","The commands run tests, parse, learn, compare and validate.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.3|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|topic:telemetry","Match each telemetry stack component to its role.",,"Telegraf","Receives the stream and forwards it","Kafka","Message bus that buffers events","InfluxDB","Time-series database","Prometheus","Scrapes and stores metrics","Grafana","Shows dashboards","These tools receive, buffer, store and display telemetry, and the choice depends on the design.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:gnmi|topic:grpc","Match each NX-OS gRPC command to its effect.",,"feature grpc","Enables the gRPC agent","grpc port","Sets the listening port","grpc certificate","Names the trustpoint for TLS","grpc use-vrf default","Lets the service answer on the default VRF","grpc gnmi max-concurrent-calls","Limits the number of simultaneous gNMI calls","The commands enable and tune the gNMI service of a Nexus switch.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:telemetry","Match each NX-OS telemetry keyword to its effect.",,"sensor-group","Holds the paths to stream","destination-group","Holds the receivers","subscription","Ties groups together with an interval","use-vrf","Chooses the VRF for the connection","source-interface","Chooses the source address of the connection","The keywords define data, destinations, schedule and the network path of dial-out telemetry.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.5|objective:cisco:350-901:2.6|topic:source-of-truth|topic:netbox","Match each NetBox feature to its use.",,"Tenant","Records which customer or team owns an object","Tag","Labels objects for grouping and filtering","Custom field","Adds an extra attribute to an object","Journal entry","A note about the history of an object","Change log","Records who changed what and when","These features organize, extend and audit the data in a source of truth.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nxapi","Match each NX-OS command to the part of the fabric it reports on.",,"show vpc","State of the vPC domain and peers","show nve peers","The VXLAN tunnel endpoints that are known","show bgp l2vpn evpn summary","The EVPN BGP sessions","show port-channel summary","The state of port channels and members","show interface status","Link state and speed of the ports","Each command reports one layer of a VXLAN EVPN fabric, which a health script can collect.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nexus-dashboard","Match each HTTP status of an API call to its likely meaning.",,"200","The request succeeded","401","The login or the token is not valid","403","The account lacks permission","404","The path or object does not exist","500","The server failed to process the request","The status codes help a script to decide whether to retry, log in again or report an error.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","Match each Docker network mode to its behavior.",,"bridge","Containers connect to a virtual bridge on the host","host","The container shares the host's network stack","none","The container has no external network","macvlan","The container gets its own MAC address on the physical network","overlay","Containers on several hosts share a virtual network","The modes decide how a container connects to the network and how visible it is.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","Match each symptom of a container network to the first thing to check.",,"The container cannot reach its gateway","The veth pair and the bridge","Only large packets are lost","The MTU along the path","Only VLAN 120 fails","The VLAN tag on the uplink","A bond member keeps flapping","LACP and the port-channel on the switch","ARP stays incomplete","Layer 2 reachability","The symptoms point to different layers, so the checks start at the veth, the MTU, the tags, the bond or Layer 2.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.1|topic:ai","Match each term used with language models in network automation to its meaning.",,"Token","A unit of text that the model processes","Embedding","A vector that represents the meaning of text","Fine-tuning","Training a model further on specific data","Grounding","Supplying facts so that the answer is based on them","Guardrail","A rule or check that limits what the system may do","The terms describe how models read text, represent it, are adapted, are kept factual and are controlled.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.2|objective:cisco:300-435:5.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.2|topic:ai|topic:ai-security","Match each attack on an AI agent to an example.",,"Indirect prompt injection","A syslog message that contains instructions","Tool poisoning","A tool description that hides harmful instructions","Data exfiltration","A secret returned in a tool output","Privilege abuse","An agent that holds administrator credentials","Denial of wallet","A loop of expensive model calls","The attacks use instructions in data, harmful tools, leaked secrets, excess rights and cost.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|topic:mcp","Match each element of an agent integration to its role.",,"MCP server","Exposes tools and data to agents","Nexus Dashboard API","Source of fabric data","NX-API","Device-level access to a switch","Webhook","An event that can trigger the agent","Secret vault","Stores the credentials that tools use","An integration connects the agent to data, devices, events and secrets through separate, controlled components.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.4|topic:ai|topic:llm-agent","Match each way of using AI in operations to its description.",,"Copilot","Suggests and a person acts","Autonomous agent","Acts without asking","Human in the loop","A person approves risky steps","Read-only analyst","Only queries and reports","Scheduled assistant","Produces reports at set times","The patterns differ in how much the AI may do on its own.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|topic:ncclient","Match each parameter of ncclient manager.connect to its meaning.",,"host","The address of the switch","port","The NETCONF port, 830 on NX-OS","username","The account that logs in","hostkey_verify","Whether the SSH host key is checked","device_params","Selects the device handler, for example nexus","The parameters say where to connect, as whom, how strictly to check the host key and which platform handler to use.",1,2

order[40]{tags,text,exhibit,s1,s2,s3,s4,s5,s6,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.1|objective:cisco:300-435:1.1|topic:yang","Place the steps of finding the path of a leaf in a YANG module in the correct order.",,"Open the module and read its prefix and namespace","Find the top-level container","Follow the containers and lists to the leaf","Note the keys of each list","Write the path with the module prefix","Check the path against the device","The module is read from its top, the path is built along the containers and keys, and the result is checked on the device.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.2|topic:aci","Place the steps of traffic from one EPG to another through a contract in the correct order.",,"A host in the consumer EPG sends a packet","The leaf identifies the source EPG","The leaf looks up the destination EPG","The contract between the EPGs is checked","The filter permits the traffic","The packet is forwarded to the destination","The fabric classifies source and destination into EPGs, checks the policy of the contract and forwards what a filter permits.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.3|topic:dpu","Place the steps of applying a security policy on a DPU in the correct order.",,"Define the policy centrally","Push it to the DPU","The DPU programs its own rules","Traffic from a workload reaches the DPU","The DPU enforces the policy at line rate","The DPU reports counters","A policy is defined and pushed, the DPU enforces it on the traffic of the workload, and results are reported.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|topic:gnmi|topic:tls","Place the steps of enabling a trusted gNMI connection in the correct order.",,"Create a trustpoint with a certificate","Enable feature grpc","Assign the certificate with grpc certificate","Trust the issuing CA on the client","Connect with gnmic","Run a capabilities request","The certificate is prepared and assigned, the client trusts its issuer, and a capabilities request proves the connection.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|objective:cisco:300-435:1.2|topic:netconf","Place the steps of a safe change through the candidate datastore in the correct order.",,"Lock the candidate","Edit the candidate","Validate it","Commit it","Unlock the candidate",,"The candidate is locked, edited, validated and committed, and the lock is released afterwards.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|objective:cisco:300-435:1.5|topic:yang|topic:pyang","Place the steps of producing a request payload with YANG tools in the correct order.",,"Load the modules into the tool","Choose the target node","Generate a skeleton of the payload","Fill in the keys and values","Validate it against the model","Send it","The tool needs the modules and the node, the skeleton is completed and validated, and then the request is sent.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.3|topic:gitops","Place the steps of onboarding a new fabric into a GitOps repository in the correct order.",,"Create the data files for the fabric","Add the playbook or Terraform configuration","Open a merge request","Review and run the validation pipeline","Merge","Let the pipeline deploy the fabric","A fabric is described in data and code, reviewed and validated, merged and deployed by the pipeline.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.3|topic:gitops|topic:secrets","Place the steps of giving a pipeline access to a fabric controller without storing the password in the repository in the correct order.",,"Store the credential in a vault or as a masked CI variable","Give the pipeline job access to it","The job reads it at run time","The job authenticates to the controller","The job output is checked to confirm that the secret is masked",,"The secret lives outside the repository, the job reads it when it runs, and the logs are checked to be sure that it does not appear.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Place the steps of debugging a template that renders the wrong configuration in the correct order.",,"Render it with a small data set","Compare the output with the expected text","Print the variables used in the failing part","Find the wrong expression or filter","Fix it and render again",,"A small case is rendered, the difference is located by inspecting the variables, and the fix is verified by rendering again.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Place the steps of a unit test for a configuration template in the correct order.",,"Store sample data and the expected output","Render the template with the sample data","Compare the result with the expected output","Fail the test on any difference","Run the test in the pipeline",,"The test needs a fixed input and output, compares the rendering and runs automatically.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible","Place the steps of a playbook that adds a VLAN to a Nexus switch in the correct order.",,"Define the inventory with the connection variables","Write the nxos_vlans task with the VLAN data","Run with --check","Review the proposed changes","Run the playbook","Run it again to confirm idempotence","The connection and the task are defined, a dry run is reviewed, and the change is applied and confirmed.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible|topic:aci","Place the steps of creating a tenant with a VRF and a bridge domain through Ansible in the correct order.",,"Create the tenant","Create the VRF in the tenant","Create the bridge domain in the tenant","Bind the bridge domain to the VRF","Verify with state query",,"The tenant comes first, the VRF and bridge domain follow, and the binding is verified with a query.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|topic:terraform","Place the steps of upgrading a provider version safely in the correct order.",,"Read the changelog of the provider","Change the version constraint","Run terraform init -upgrade","Run terraform plan and review it","Apply when the plan shows no unexpected changes",,"The release notes are read, the version is changed, the provider is downloaded, and the plan is reviewed before the apply.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|topic:terraform","Place the steps of splitting a resource into a module without recreating it in the correct order.",,"Create the module with the resource block","Move the resource address with terraform state mv","Call the module in the root configuration","Run terraform plan","Confirm that no resource is replaced",,"The state address is moved to match the new module path, and the plan must show no replacement.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|topic:ansible|topic:troubleshooting","Place the steps of finding why an Ansible task fails only on one switch in the correct order.",,"Run with -vvv limited to that host","Check the connection variables of the host","Test the login manually","Compare the platform or version with the working hosts","Fix the host variable or the account",,"The run is narrowed to the failing host, its variables and login are checked, and it is compared with working hosts.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|topic:terraform|topic:troubleshooting","Place the steps of recovering from a lost Terraform state in the correct order.",,"Find the last good state backup","Restore it to the backend","Run terraform state list","Run terraform plan","Import objects that are missing from the state","Apply when the plan shows no unwanted change","The backup is restored first, the contents are checked, and missing objects are imported before an apply.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|topic:ncclient","Place the steps of reading part of the configuration with ncclient and a filter in the correct order.",,"Connect with manager.connect","Build the subtree filter XML","Call get_config with the filter","Read the XML reply","Parse the values you need",,"A session is opened, the filter is built and applied, and the reply is parsed.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|topic:ncclient","Place the steps of error handling around an edit_config call in the correct order.",,"Open the session in a with block","Call edit_config inside a try block","Catch RPCError and read its message","Log the error with the device name","Close the session when the block ends",,"The call is protected by try, errors are caught and logged, and the session closes automatically.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap|topic:troubleshooting","Place the steps of troubleshooting a POAP that does not start the script in the correct order.",,"Check the DHCP offer for option 67","Check the TFTP or HTTP server and the script file","Check the DHCP lease time","Check the script's MD5 line","Restart POAP",,"The offer, the file server, the lease and the checksum are checked before POAP is restarted.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap","Place the steps of publishing a new image for POAP in the correct order.",,"Copy the image to the file server","Create its .md5 file","Set the image name in the script","Update the MD5 line of the script","Boot a test switch with POAP",,"The image and its checksum are published, the script is updated and its own checksum is recalculated, and a test switch confirms the process.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|objective:cisco:300-435:2.7|topic:python|topic:on-box","Place the steps of a script that backs up the running configuration on the switch in the correct order.",,"Import the cli module","Call cli('show running-config')","Write the text to a file in bootflash","Add a timestamp to the file name","Copy the file to a server",,"The script reads the configuration, stores it under a unique name and copies it off the switch.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|objective:cisco:300-435:2.7|topic:guest-shell","Place the steps of installing a Python package in the Guest Shell in the correct order.",,"Enable the Guest Shell","Give it network access and a DNS server","Open it with guestshell run bash","Install the package with pip","Run a script that uses it",,"The container is enabled and connected before a package is installed and used.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.4|topic:ndfc|topic:templates","Place the stages of the life of a policy in Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller in the correct order.",,"Choose a template","Fill in the variables","Attach the policy to the switches","Preview the configuration","Deploy","Check the result","A policy is created from a template, attached, previewed and deployed, and the result is checked.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.5|topic:ndfc|topic:templates","Place the steps of testing a new template in Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller in the correct order.",,"Write the template","Validate its syntax","Create a policy for a lab switch","Preview the generated CLI","Deploy it to the lab switch","Use it for production switches","The template is validated and tried on a lab switch before it is used in production.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Place the steps of sending configuration commands with rollback through NX-API CLI in the correct order.",,"Enable feature nxapi","Build a cli_conf request with the commands","Set the rollback option","POST it to /ins","Read the code and msg of each output",,"The service is enabled, the request carries the commands and the error action, and the outputs are read.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Place the steps of changing an interface description with NX-API REST in the correct order.",,"Log in with aaaLogin","Build the JSON body for the interface object","POST it to the object's path","Check the status code","Read the object again",,"A session is obtained, the object is changed by a POST to its path, and the result is verified.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:2.4|topic:cml|topic:simulation","Place the steps of a regression test of a fabric change in CML in the correct order.",,"Start the lab with the current configuration","Run the baseline tests","Apply the change","Run the tests again","Compare the results","Tear down the lab","A baseline is taken, the change is applied, the tests run again and the results are compared before the lab is removed.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:3.4|objective:cisco:300-435:4.1|topic:pyats","Place the steps of building a pyATS health check in the correct order.",,"Write the testbed","Choose the commands to parse","Write the checks on the parsed data","Run the job","Read the report",,"The testbed and checks are prepared before the job runs and the report is read.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.3|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|topic:telemetry","Place the steps of planning a telemetry design in the correct order.",,"List the questions that the data must answer","Choose the sensor paths","Choose the interval or on-change","Size the collector and the database","Build the dashboards and alerts",,"The questions decide the data, the schedule and the capacity before dashboards are built.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:gnmi|topic:telemetry","Place the steps of testing a gNMI subscription with gnmic in the correct order.",,"Run gnmic capabilities","Choose a path from the supported models","Run gnmic get on the path","Run gnmic subscribe with a sample interval","Check that updates arrive",,"Capabilities shows the models, a path is chosen and read once, and then streamed.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:telemetry","Place the steps of verifying a dial-out subscription on NX-OS in the correct order.",,"Check the subscription configuration","Check that the receiver is reachable from the switch","Check the state of the subscription on the switch","Check that data arrives at the collector","Compare the values with the CLI",,"The configuration, the path to the receiver, the subscription state and the data are checked, and the values are compared with the CLI.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.5|objective:cisco:350-901:2.6|topic:source-of-truth|topic:netbox","Place the steps of reconciling a fabric with NetBox in the correct order.",,"Read the intended data from NetBox","Collect the actual state from the switches","Compare the two","Report the differences","Correct the devices or the record through a reviewed change",,"Intent and reality are compared, the differences are reported, and a reviewed change corrects them.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nxapi","Place the steps of a script that checks the health of all switches in the correct order.",,"Read the list of switches","Send show system resources to each switch","Send show environment to each switch","Compare the values with thresholds","Report the switches over a threshold",,"The switches are listed, data is collected from each, compared and the exceptions are reported.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nexus-dashboard","Place the steps of a script that reads data from Nexus Dashboard in the correct order.",,"Log in to /login","Store the token","Call the API with the token","Check the status code","Renew the token when it expires",,"The script logs in, calls the API with the token, checks the answers and renews the token.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","Place the steps of tracing a packet from a container to a switch in the correct order.",,"Capture on the container's interface","Capture on the host end of the veth","Capture on the bridge","Capture on the uplink and check the VLAN tag","Capture on the switch port",,"A packet is followed from the container to the switch to find where it disappears.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","Place the steps of creating a VLAN subinterface and attaching it to a bridge in the correct order.",,"Create the subinterface on the uplink with a VLAN ID","Bring it up","Create the bridge","Attach the subinterface to the bridge","Attach the veth ends of the containers to the bridge",,"The subinterface and the bridge are created, joined, and the containers are connected to the bridge.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.1|topic:ai","Place the steps of getting a good first draft of a template from an AI assistant in the correct order.",,"Describe the platform and the goal","Provide an example of the data","Ask for the template","Review the draft","Render and test it",,"The assistant needs context and an example, and its draft is reviewed and tested.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.2|objective:cisco:300-435:5.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.2|topic:ai|topic:ai-security","Place the steps of protecting an agent against secrets in tool output in the correct order.",,"List the data that a tool returns","Remove or mask the secrets","Return only the fields that are needed","Log the call without the secrets","Test with a sample that contains secrets",,"The output is inspected, cleaned and reduced before it reaches the model, and a test confirms it.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|topic:mcp","Place the steps of exposing fabric health to an agent through MCP in the correct order.",,"Create a read-only account","Write a tool that calls the API","Return only the needed fields","Run the server","Connect the agent and test the tool",,"The account and the tool are prepared with least privilege, and the agent is connected after the server runs.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.4|topic:ai|topic:llm-agent","Place the steps of adding human approval to an agent that can change configuration in the correct order.",,"Split read tools and write tools","Let the agent propose a change","Show the proposed change to a person","The person approves or rejects it","Apply the approved change","Log the result","The agent proposes and a person approves before the change is applied and logged.",3,2

slotfill[40]{tags,text,exhibit,a1,a2,a3,a4,a5,d1,d2,d3,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.1|objective:cisco:300-435:1.1|topic:openconfig|topic:gnmi","Fill in each blank so that gnmic reads the administrative status of Ethernet1/1 from the OpenConfig model and asks for IETF JSON values.","```bash\ngnmic -a 192.0.2.11:50051 -u admin -p 'C1sco123' --skip-verify get --path /interfaces/interface[name=⟦1⟧]/state/⟦2⟧ --encoding ⟦3⟧\n```","Ethernet1/1","admin-status","json_ietf",,,"oper-status","json","proto","The list entry is addressed by its key, the state container holds read-only values such as admin-status, and json_ietf asks for IETF-style JSON. oper-status is the operational status, and json and proto are other encodings.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.2|topic:aci","Fill in each blank with the ACI class that creates a filter entry, a contract and a contract subject.","```json\n{\"vzFilter\": {\"attributes\": {\"name\": \"web\"}, \"children\": [\n  {\"⟦1⟧\": {\"attributes\": {\"name\": \"https\", \"etherT\": \"ip\", \"prot\": \"tcp\", \"dFromPort\": \"https\", \"dToPort\": \"https\"}}}]}}\n\n{\"⟦2⟧\": {\"attributes\": {\"name\": \"web-ct\"}, \"children\": [\n  {\"⟦3⟧\": {\"attributes\": {\"name\": \"web-subj\"}}}]}}\n```","vzEntry","vzBrCP","vzSubj",,,"fvAEPg","vzAny","vzTaboo","A filter holds entries, a contract is vzBrCP, and a subject is vzSubj. fvAEPg is an EPG, vzAny stands for all EPGs of a VRF, and vzTaboo is a taboo contract.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.3|topic:dpu|topic:sr-iov","Fill in each blank so that eight virtual functions are created on a network card and the first one is placed in VLAN 120.","```bash\necho 8 > /sys/class/net/eth0/device/⟦1⟧\nip link set eth0 vf 0 ⟦2⟧ 120\n```","sriov_numvfs","vlan",,,,"numvfs","vid","sriov","The sriov_numvfs file sets the number of virtual functions, and ip link set with vf and vlan assigns a VLAN to one of them. The other names are not part of these commands.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|topic:gnmi|topic:grpc","Fill in each blank so that pygnmi connects to the default gNMI port, skips verification of the certificate, and asks for the capabilities.","```python\nfrom pygnmi.client import gNMIclient\n\nwith gNMIclient(target=('192.0.2.11', ⟦1⟧), username='admin', password='C1sco123', ⟦2⟧=True) as gc:\n    caps = gc.⟦3⟧()\n```","50051","skip_verify","capabilities",,,"830","insecure","get","The NX-OS gNMI service listens on 50051 by default, skip_verify accepts a self-signed certificate, and capabilities asks for the supported models. 830 is NETCONF, insecure turns TLS off, and get reads values.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|objective:cisco:300-435:1.2|topic:netconf","Fill in each blank so that the RPC reads the configuration from the running datastore.","```xml\n<rpc message-id=\"101\" xmlns=\"urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:netconf:base:1.0\">\n  <⟦1⟧>\n    <source><⟦2⟧/></source>\n  </⟦1⟧>\n</rpc>\n```","get-config","running",,,,"get","startup","copy-config","get-config reads configuration from a datastore, and the source names the running datastore. get also returns state, startup is another datastore, and copy-config copies a datastore.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:pyang|topic:yang","Fill in each blank so that pyang prints the text tree of a module down to two levels.","```bash\npyang -f ⟦1⟧ --tree-depth ⟦2⟧ cisco-nx-os-device.yang\n```","tree","2",,,,"jstree","20","yin","The tree format prints the module tree, and --tree-depth limits its depth. jstree creates an HTML tree, and yin converts the module to XML syntax.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.3|topic:gitops|topic:gitlab-ci","Fill in each blank so that the deployment job is tracked as an environment and waits until a person starts it.","```yaml\ndeploy-fabric:\n  stage: deploy\n  ⟦1⟧:\n    name: production\n  rules:\n    - if: '$CI_COMMIT_BRANCH == \"main\"'\n      when: ⟦2⟧\n```","environment","manual",,,,"stage","on_success","always","An environment entry tracks deployments, and when manual makes the job wait for a person. on_success and always run the job without waiting.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.1|topic:gitops|topic:git","Fill in each blank to undo the last commit with a new commit and publish it so that the pipeline redeploys the previous state.","```bash\ngit ⟦1⟧ HEAD\ngit ⟦2⟧ origin main\n```","revert","push",,,,"reset","pull","checkout","revert creates a commit that undoes another, and push publishes it. reset rewrites history, pull fetches, and checkout switches.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Fill in each blank so that the loop walks over the names and values of a dictionary, and the ID list is built from the values and sorted.","```jinja\n{% for name, vlan in vlans.⟦1⟧() %}\nvlan {{ vlan.id }}\n  name {{ name }}\n{% endfor %}\n{{ vlans.values() | ⟦2⟧(attribute='id') | ⟦3⟧ }}\n```","items","map","sort",,,"keys","selectattr","unique","items yields key and value pairs, map extracts the attribute from every value, and sort orders the result. keys gives only names, selectattr filters, and unique removes duplicates.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Fill in each blank so that the template defines a reusable macro with a default mask and closes it.","```jinja\n{% ⟦1⟧ svi(id, ip, mask='255.255.255.0') %}\ninterface Vlan{{ id }}\n ip address {{ ip }} {{ mask }}\n{% ⟦2⟧ %}\n{{ svi(10, '10.0.10.1') }}\n```","macro","endmacro",,,,"def","endfor","call","A macro is defined with macro and closed with endmacro, and it is used like a function. def is not Jinja2 syntax, and endfor and call do not close a macro.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible","Fill in each blank so that the task manages the attributes of interfaces on a Nexus switch and adds the listed values to what exists.","```yaml\n- cisco.nxos.nxos_⟦1⟧:\n    config:\n      - name: Ethernet1/1\n        description: uplink\n        enabled: true\n    state: ⟦2⟧\n```","interfaces","merged",,,,"vlans","gathered","parsed","The nxos_interfaces module manages interface attributes, and merged adds or updates the listed values. nxos_vlans manages VLANs, and gathered and parsed only read.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible|topic:aci","Fill in each blank so that the EPG is created and the certificate of the lab APIC is not verified.","```yaml\n- cisco.aci.aci_epg:\n    host: apic.example.com\n    username: admin\n    password: \"{{ vault_pw }}\"\n    tenant: Prod\n    ap: shop\n    epg: web\n    bd: web-bd\n    state: ⟦1⟧\n    validate_certs: ⟦2⟧\n```","present","false",,,,"query","true","absent","state present creates the EPG, and validate_certs false accepts the self-signed certificate of a lab. query only reads, absent deletes, and true would verify the certificate.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|topic:terraform","Fill in each blank so that the state is kept in an S3 bucket and locked through a DynamoDB table.","```hcl\nterraform {\n  backend \"⟦1⟧\" {\n    bucket         = \"net-state\"\n    key            = \"fabric1/terraform.tfstate\"\n    region         = \"eu-west-1\"\n    ⟦2⟧ = \"tf-locks\"\n  }\n}\n```","s3","dynamodb_table",,,,"gcs","lock_table","state_lock","The s3 backend stores the state in a bucket, and dynamodb_table names the table that provides locking. gcs is another backend, and the other names are not arguments.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|topic:terraform|topic:aci","Fill in each blank so that the VRF uses the DN of an existing tenant that was read with a data source.","```hcl\ndata \"aci_tenant\" \"common\" {\n  name = \"common\"\n}\n\nresource \"aci_vrf\" \"main\" {\n  tenant_dn = data.⟦1⟧.common.⟦2⟧\n  name      = \"main\"\n}\n```","aci_tenant","id",,,,"aci_vrf","name","resource","A data source is referenced as data.TYPE.NAME.ATTRIBUTE, and the id of an ACI object is its DN. aci_vrf is the other resource, and name is only the short name.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|topic:ansible|topic:troubleshooting","Fill in each blank to run the playbook only for leaf1 and to list its tasks without running them.","```bash\nansible-playbook site.yml --⟦1⟧ leaf1 --⟦2⟧\n```","limit","list-tasks",,,,"tags","check","syntax-check","--limit selects the hosts and --list-tasks prints the tasks without running them. --tags selects tasks, --check is a dry run, and --syntax-check only parses the playbook.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|topic:terraform|topic:troubleshooting","Fill in each blank to write a debug log of the provider calls and then preview the changes.","```bash\nexport ⟦1⟧=DEBUG\nexport TF_LOG_PATH=./tf.log\nterraform ⟦2⟧\n```","TF_LOG","plan",,,,"TF_DEBUG","apply","init","TF_LOG sets the log level of Terraform and its providers, and plan previews the changes. TF_DEBUG is not a variable, and apply and init do other things.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|topic:ncclient","Fill in each blank so that the filter selects the native NX-OS model, and the call returns both configuration and state.","```python\nflt = '<System xmlns=\"http://cisco.com/ns/yang/⟦1⟧\"/>'\nreply = m.⟦2⟧(('subtree', flt))\n```","cisco-nx-os-device","get",,,,"openconfig","edit_config","ietf","The native NX-OS model has the namespace cisco-nx-os-device, and get returns configuration and state. edit_config changes configuration.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|topic:ncclient","Fill in each blank so that ncclient logs in with a key file, checks the host key, and does not use an SSH agent.","```python\nm = manager.connect(host=h, port=830, username=u, ⟦1⟧='/home/ops/.ssh/id_rsa', hostkey_verify=⟦2⟧, allow_agent=⟦3⟧)\n```","key_filename","True","False",,,"pkey","None","ssh_key","key_filename names the private key, hostkey_verify True checks the host key, and allow_agent False disables the agent. pkey and ssh_key are not the parameter names.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap","Fill in each blank so that the DHCP server names the TFTP server and gives a lease that POAP can complete.","```text\nsubnet 10.20.0.0 netmask 255.255.255.0 {\n  range 10.20.0.100 10.20.0.200;\n  option ⟦2⟧ \"10.20.0.5\";\n  option bootfile-name \"poap.py\";\n  default-lease-time ⟦1⟧;\n}\n```","3600","tftp-server-name",,,,"600","tftp-server","next-server","POAP needs a lease of at least 3600 seconds, and the TFTP server is named in the tftp-server-name option. A short lease fails, and the other names are not options.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap","Fill in each blank so that the checksum line of the script is excluded, and the copy is stored with the extension that the switch checks.","```bash\nf=poap.py ; cat $f | sed '/^#⟦1⟧/d' > $f.⟦2⟧\n```","md5sum","md5",,,,"checksum","sha256","tmp","The script's header line starts with #md5sum, and the checksum is calculated over a copy that has the extension .md5 and no such line. The other names are not used.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|objective:cisco:300-435:2.7|topic:python|topic:on-box","Fill in each blank so that the on-box function returns the names of the interfaces that are down.","```python\nfrom cli import *\nimport json\n\ndef down_interfaces():\n    # Purpose: return the names of interfaces that are down\n    data = json.loads(⟦1⟧('show interface brief'))\n    rows = data['TABLE_interface']['⟦2⟧']\n    return [r['interface'] for r in rows if r.get('state') == '⟦3⟧']\n```","clid","ROW_interface","down",,,"cli","ROW_intf","up","clid returns JSON text, the rows are in ROW_interface below TABLE_interface, and the state down selects the interfaces that are down. cli returns text, and up selects the wrong ones.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|topic:bash","Fill in each blank so that the Bash script on the switch saves the configuration with a time stamp.","```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# Purpose: save the running configuration with a time stamp\nts=$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)\n⟦1⟧ \"show running-config\" > /bootflash/backup-$ts.⟦2⟧\n```","vsh -c","cfg",,,,"nxcli","show","tmp","The vsh command runs an NX-OS command from Bash, and the output is saved with a name that ends in .cfg. nxcli and show are not Bash commands, and tmp is a poor extension for a backup.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.4|topic:ndfc|topic:templates","Fill in each blank so that the policy is created from the template that sets the BGP AS and gives its value.","```json\n{\n  \"templateName\": \"⟦1⟧\",\n  \"nvPairs\": {\"⟦2⟧\": \"65000.4\"}\n}\n```","leaf_bgp_asn","BGP_AS",,,,"leaf_bgp","ASN","bgp_asn","The built-in template is named leaf_bgp_asn and takes the variable BGP_AS. The other names are not the template or its variable.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.5|topic:ndfc|topic:templates","Fill in each blank so that the template is a policy with CLI content.","```text\n##template properties\nname = banner_policy;\ntemplateType = ⟦1⟧;\ncontentType = ⟦2⟧;\n##\n```","POLICY","TEMPLATE_CLI",,,,"PROFILE","TEMPLATE_PYTHON","CLI_TEMPLATE","A policy template has the type POLICY, and CLI content has the content type TEMPLATE_CLI. PROFILE is used for networks and VRFs, and the other values do not exist.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Fill in each blank so that two commands are sent in one request, and all are undone if one fails.","```json\n{\"ins_api\": {\"version\": \"1.0\", \"type\": \"⟦2⟧\", \"chunk\": \"0\", \"sid\": \"1\",\n  \"input\": \"interface Ethernet1/1 ⟦1⟧ description uplink\", \"output_format\": \"json\", \"rollback\": \"⟦3⟧\"}}\n```",";","cli_conf","rollback-on-error",,,",","cli_show","stop-on-error","NX-API CLI separates commands with a semicolon, configuration uses the cli_conf type, and rollback-on-error undoes the commands that were applied. cli_show is for show commands, and stop-on-error leaves the earlier changes in place.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Fill in each blank so that the request changes the description of a physical interface with NX-API REST.","```text\nPOST /api/mo/sys/intf/phys-[⟦3⟧].json\n{\"⟦1⟧\": {\"attributes\": {\"⟦2⟧\": \"uplink\"}}}\n```","l1PhysIf","descr","eth1/1",,,"ethpmPhysIf","description","ethernet1/1","The class l1PhysIf is the physical interface, its attribute descr holds the description, and the DN uses the short name eth1/1. The other values are not the class, the attribute or the name.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:2.4|topic:cml|topic:simulation","Fill in each blank so that the script saves the pyATS testbed of a lab and finds a node by its label.","```python\ntb = lab.⟦1⟧()\nopen('tb.yaml', 'w').write(tb)\nleaf1 = lab.⟦2⟧('leaf1')\n```","get_pyats_testbed","get_node_by_label",,,,"export_testbed","get_node","find_node","The lab object returns a pyATS testbed and finds a node by its label with these methods. The other names are not methods.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.2|topic:pyats","Fill in each blank so that the testbed describes an NX-OS device that is reached over SSH.","```yaml\ndevices:\n  leaf1:\n    os: ⟦1⟧\n    type: switch\n    connections:\n      cli:\n        protocol: ⟦2⟧\n        ip: 192.0.2.21\n```","nxos","ssh",,,,"iosxe","telnet","netconf","The os key selects the parser and plugin set, here nxos, and the protocol ssh uses an encrypted session. iosxe is another platform, telnet is not encrypted, and netconf is not a CLI protocol.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.3|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|topic:telemetry|topic:gnmi","Fill in each blank so that gnmic prints flat events that suit a time-series database, and the stream sends a value only when it changes.","```bash\ngnmic -a 192.0.2.11:50051 -u admin -p 'C1sco123' --skip-verify subscribe --path /interfaces/interface/state/counters --format ⟦1⟧ --stream-mode ⟦2⟧\n```","event","on-change",,,,"json","sample","once","The event format flattens updates into events with names, tags and values, and on-change sends an update when a value changes. json is a nested format, and sample and once are other modes.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:gnmi|topic:grpc","Fill in each blank to allow 16 simultaneous gNMI calls, answer on the default VRF, and change the listening port.","```text\nswitch(config)# grpc gnmi max-concurrent-calls ⟦1⟧\nswitch(config)# grpc use-vrf ⟦2⟧\nswitch(config)# grpc ⟦3⟧ 50052\n```","16","default","port",,,"1000","management","certificate","max-concurrent-calls takes the number of calls, use-vrf default adds the default VRF, and grpc port sets the port. The management VRF is served by default, and certificate names a trustpoint.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:gnmi|topic:nxos-native","Fill in each blank so that gnmic reads the BGP router ID of the default domain from the native model.","```bash\ngnmic -a 192.0.2.11:50051 -u admin -p 'C1sco123' --skip-verify get --path /System/⟦1⟧-items/inst-items/dom-items/Dom-list/⟦2⟧\n```","bgp","rtrId",,,,"ospf","routerId","eigrp","The native model path goes through bgp-items and the domain list, and rtrId is the router ID attribute. The other names belong to other protocols or do not exist.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.5|objective:cisco:350-901:2.6|topic:source-of-truth|topic:netbox","Fill in each blank so that the script creates a device, reads it again, and stores a changed status.","```python\nnb = pynetbox.api(url, token=token)\nnb.dcim.devices.⟦1⟧(name='leaf1', role=1, device_type=2, site=3)\ndev = nb.dcim.devices.⟦2⟧(name='leaf1')\ndev.status = 'active'\ndev.⟦3⟧()\n```","create","get","save",,,"add","all","update","create adds an object, get returns exactly one, and save stores the attributes that were changed on the object. add and all are not the right calls, and update needs a dictionary.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nexus-dashboard","Fill in each blank so that the call sends the token in the cookie that Nexus Dashboard expects and accepts the lab certificate.","```python\nr = requests.get(url, cookies={'⟦1⟧': token}, verify=⟦2⟧)\n```","AuthCookie","False",,,,"JSESSIONID","True","session","Nexus Dashboard accepts the token from the login in the AuthCookie cookie, and verify=False accepts a self-signed lab certificate. JSESSIONID is used by other products, and True would reject the certificate.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nxapi","Fill in each blank so that ten switches are checked in parallel and the results are collected in order.","```python\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\n\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=⟦1⟧) as pool:\n    results = list(pool.⟦2⟧(check, switches))\n```","10","map",,,,"1000","submit","shutdown","max_workers sets the number of threads, and map runs the function for every switch and returns the results in order. 1000 threads would be wasteful, and submit and shutdown do other things.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","Fill in each blank so that the bridge filters by VLAN, and the host end of the veth carries VLAN 120 as the untagged default.","```bash\nip link add br0 type bridge vlan_filtering ⟦1⟧\nbridge vlan add dev veth-h0 vid ⟦2⟧ ⟦3⟧ untagged\n```","1","120","pvid",,,"0","100","tagged","vlan_filtering 1 switches on VLAN handling, vid names the VLAN, and pvid untagged makes it the default for untagged frames. 0 would leave filtering off, 100 is another VLAN, and tagged is not a keyword.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","Fill in each blank to set the MTU of a VLAN subinterface and to read the state of a bond.","```bash\nip link set dev bond0.120 ⟦1⟧ 9000\ncat /proc/net/⟦2⟧/bond0\n```","mtu","bonding",,,,"mss","bond","bridge","The ip link command sets the mtu, and the bonding directory of /proc/net holds the state of each bond. mss is a TCP setting, and the other directory names do not exist.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.1|topic:ai|topic:llm","Fill in each blank so that the model answers in JSON and gives the same answer for the same prompt as far as possible.","```python\nresp = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model='m', messages=messages,\n    response_format={'type': '⟦1⟧'},\n    temperature=⟦2⟧,\n)\n```","json_object","0",,,,"json","1","text","The json_object format makes the model return valid JSON, and a temperature of 0 reduces randomness. json is not the type name, 1 adds randomness, and text is plain text.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.2|objective:cisco:300-435:5.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.2|topic:ai|topic:ai-security","Fill in each blank so that only read-only commands pass the check after the text is cleaned.","```python\nALLOWED = ('show ', 'ping ')\n\ndef check(cmd):\n    # Purpose: allow only read-only commands from an agent\n    cmd = cmd.⟦2⟧().lower()\n    if not cmd.⟦1⟧(ALLOWED) or ';' in cmd:\n        raise PermissionError(cmd)\n```","startswith","strip",,,,"endswith","split","find","strip removes surrounding spaces, and startswith accepts a tuple of allowed prefixes. endswith checks the wrong end, and split and find do not test a prefix.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|topic:mcp|topic:fastmcp","Fill in each blank so that the client lists the tools of a server and calls one of them.","```python\nimport asyncio\nfrom fastmcp import Client\n\nasync def main():\n    async with Client('http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp') as c:\n        tools = await c.⟦1⟧()\n        r = await c.⟦2⟧('cpu_idle', {'switch': 'leaf1'})\n```","list_tools","call_tool",,,,"get_tools","run_tool","invoke","The client lists the tools with list_tools and calls one with call_tool and its arguments. The other names are not methods of the client.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.1|topic:ai|topic:embeddings","Fill in each blank so that the function returns the cosine similarity of two embedding vectors.","```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef similarity(a, b):\n    # Purpose: return the cosine similarity of two embedding vectors\n    return float(np.⟦1⟧(a, b) / (np.linalg.⟦2⟧(a) * np.linalg.norm(b)))\n```","dot","norm",,,,"cross","det","inv","The cosine similarity is the dot product divided by the product of the lengths of the vectors, and the norm gives the length. cross, det and inv are other operations.",3,3
